@model CrossBuy.BL.Portal.PortalHome
@using System.Globalization
@*
    HOME — Metronic demo30's dashboard (index.html): its hero band, its content menu, its stat cards
    and its table widgets, all kept.

    What the theme fills those components with is web analytics — organic sessions, referral sources,
    top queries, visits by source, department stats — and the platform has nothing behind any of it
    for a customer. Rather than leave a customer's home page showing someone else's numbers, the
    widgets that had no answer were taken out and the ones that did were filled from
    IPortalDataService: three figures and the two recent lists, in the theme's own stat card and
    table-widget markup.

    Ask for any of the removed widgets back and it returns the moment there is a real series behind
    it. What is NOT coming back by itself: anything aggregating other customers.
*@
@{
    Layout = null;
    var isAr = CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture.TwoLetterISOLanguageName == "ar";
}
